    <bpmn:process id="W_W1920" name="W1920. Price Sensitivity &amp; Elasticity Research by Category" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual pricing strategy review; significant cost change; competitive pricing pressure
Frequency: Annual per key category; ad-hoc for pricing decisions
Volume: Top 8 categories by revenue (representing ~80% of revenue)
Owner: FP&amp;A
Participants: FP&amp;A, Category Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1920 — Price Sensitivity &amp; Elasticity Research by Category</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1920_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1920_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1920_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1920_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1920_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1920_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1920_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1920_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1920_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1920_Start5" name="Annual pricing strategy review; significant cost change; competitive pricing pressure">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1920_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1920_Task6" name="FP&amp;A analyzes price elasticity using historical data: (a) Van Westendorp price…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A analyzes price elasticity using historical data: (a) Van Westendorp price sensitivity analysis: survey customers on what they consider too cheap, cheap, expensive, and too expensive for key products in each category, (b) historical price-volume analysis: when BuildRight changed prices in the past, what was the volume impact? (c) competitive price positioning: BuildRight&#x27;s price relative to competitors and corresponding market share, (d) segment analysis: are trade professionals more price-sensitive than DIY customers? (e) category elasticity ranking: which categories are most/least price-sensitive?
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 3–5 days/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1920_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1920_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1920_Task7" name="Category Manager applies elasticity insights to pricing strategy: (a) for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager applies elasticity insights to pricing strategy: (a) for elastic categories (price-sensitive): maintain competitive pricing; use promotions to drive volume; avoid price increases unless cost-pass-through is necessary, (b) for inelastic categories (price-insensitive): optimize margin; premium positioning where quality perception supports it, (c) for trade vs. DIY: differentiated pricing — trade accounts get quantity discounts; DIY customers pay SRP
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1920_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1920_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1920_Task8" name="VP Merchandising approves pricing strategy adjustments per W40 (price change…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Merchandising approves pricing strategy adjustments per W40 (price change execution)
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per W40</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1920_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1920_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1920_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1920_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-375 (ensure controlled execution — Product Category &amp; Shopper Research (PA-44.3).) | - operational: FP&amp;A review and approval gate
Owner: FP&amp;A</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1920_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1920_Annotation10" targetRef="W1920_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
