    <bpmn:process id="W_W1921" name="W1921. Seasonal Demand Pattern Analysis &amp; Forecast Calibration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual seasonal planning cycle (pre-summer, pre-rainy, pre-Ber months)
Frequency: Annual analysis; quarterly calibration
Volume: All 13 product categories with seasonal patterns
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Market Research Analyst, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1921 — Seasonal Demand Pattern Analysis &amp; Forecast Calibration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1921_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1921_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1921_Lane2" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1921_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1921_Start4" name="Annual seasonal planning cycle (pre-summer, pre-rainy, pre-Ber months)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1921_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1921_Task5" name="Merchandise Planner analyzes seasonal demand patterns: (a) 3-year monthly sales…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandise Planner analyzes seasonal demand patterns: (a) 3-year monthly sales by category: identify seasonal peaks and troughs, (b) peak categories: paint and tiles (Jan–Feb dry season), garden and outdoor (Mar–Apr summer), waterproofing (Jun–Aug rainy), appliances and décor (Sep–Dec Ber months), (c) calculate seasonal indices: monthly sales as multiple of average monthly sales, (d) identify external drivers: typhoon events (spike in repair materials), government infrastructure spending timing, OFW remittance peaks (Dec), (e) regional variation: Mindanao dry season differs from Luzon; adjust seasonal indices by region
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1921_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1921_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1921_Task6" name="Market Research Analyst provides forward-looking indicators: (a) PAGASA weather…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Market Research Analyst provides forward-looking indicators: (a) PAGASA weather forecast: El Niño/La Niña cycle impacts construction and renovation timing, (b) PSA construction permit trends: leading indicator for contractor demand, (c) consumer sentiment survey data: planned home improvement projects, (d) competitor promotional calendar intelligence: when are competitors running major sales?
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1921_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1921_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1921_Task7" name="Merchandise Planner adjusts demand forecast with seasonal factors: (a) apply…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandise Planner adjusts demand forecast with seasonal factors: (a) apply seasonal indices to annual forecast, (b) adjust for known events (e.g., stronger La Niña → higher waterproofing demand), (c) coordinate with Buyer for seasonal inventory buildup per W2, (d) coordinate with VP Merchandising for seasonal promotional calendar per W14
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1921_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1921_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1921_Task8" name="Quarterly: Merchandise Planner compares actual demand to seasonal forecast: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly: Merchandise Planner compares actual demand to seasonal forecast: (a) forecast accuracy by category, (b) identify categories where actual deviated significantly from forecast — investigate cause, (c) recalibrate seasonal indices based on actuals
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1921_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1921_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1921_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
