    <bpmn:process id="W_W1922" name="W1922. DIY vs. Trade Professional Shopper Segment Research" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual segment analysis; category strategy requiring segment understanding
Frequency: Annual comprehensive analysis
Volume: 2 primary segments (DIY homeowner, trade professional) + corporate buyer sub-segment
Owner: Market Research Analyst
Participants: Market Research Analyst, Category Manager, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1922 — DIY vs. Trade Professional Shopper Segment Research</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1922_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1922_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1922_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1922_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1922_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1922_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1922_Lane3" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1922_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1922_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1922_Start5" name="Annual segment analysis; category strategy requiring segment understanding">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1922_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1922_Task6" name="Market Research Analyst profiles DIY vs. trade segments: (a) average…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Market Research Analyst profiles DIY vs. trade segments: (a) average transaction value: DIY ~PHP 800–1,500; trade ~PHP 5,000–15,000; corporate ~PHP 50,000–500,000, (b) purchase frequency: DIY ~2–4 visits/month; trade ~4–8 visits/month; corporate ~1–2 visits/month but larger orders, (c) category preferences: DIY → paint, hand tools, garden, décor; trade → lumber, cement, plumbing, electrical, hardware, (d) purchase drivers: DIY → home improvement project, renovation, repair; trade → construction project requirements, (e) decision-making: DIY → influenced by price, brand, Sales Associate recommendation; trade → influenced by specification, availability, credit terms, (f) channel preference: DIY → open to ecommerce; trade → prefer in-store with account card; corporate → prefer account manager + delivery
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1922_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1922_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1922_Task7" name="Category Manager applies segment insights: (a) store-level assortment tuning…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager applies segment insights: (a) store-level assortment tuning: stores near residential areas stock more DIY-friendly products; stores near construction sites stock more trade-oriented products, (b) marketing message differentiation: DIY messaging focuses on project inspiration and ease; trade messaging focuses on specification, availability, and pricing, (c) service differentiation: DIY customers need more associate guidance; trade customers need fast checkout and account access, (d) cross-selling: DIY customer buying paint → suggest brushes, tarps, tape; trade customer buying cement → suggest rebar, sand, gravel
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1922_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1922_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1922_Task8" name="VP Store Operations applies segment insights to store staffing and layout: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Store Operations applies segment insights to store staffing and layout: (a) stores with high trade traffic: allocate more experienced associates to trade-heavy departments, (b) stores with high DIY traffic: allocate associates with strong customer service skills, (c) adjust store hours if trade segment prefers early morning visits
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1922_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1922_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1922_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
