    <bpmn:process id="W_W1924" name="W1924. Store Layout &amp; Category Adjacency Effectiveness Research" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual planogram refresh; new store layout design; renovation
Frequency: Annual analysis; per new store design
Volume: Per store format
Owner: VP Store Operations
Participants: VP Store Operations, Market Research Analyst, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1924 — Store Layout &amp; Category Adjacency Effectiveness Research</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1924_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1924_Lane1" name="Market Research Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1924_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1924_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1924_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1924_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1924_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1924_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1924_Start4" name="Annual planogram refresh; new store layout design; renovation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1924_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1924_Task5" name="Market Research Analyst analyzes category adjacency effectiveness: (a) basket…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Market Research Analyst analyzes category adjacency effectiveness: (a) basket analysis: which categories are most frequently bought together? (these should be adjacent or connected), (b) sales per sqm by department: which departments generate the highest/lowest revenue per sqm? (consider expanding high-productivity departments and reducing low-productivity), (c) traffic flow analysis: what % of customers visit each department? Are there dead zones where traffic is low?, (d) trade vs. DIY adjacency: trade-focused departments (lumber, plumbing, electrical) should be clustered; DIY departments (paint, décor, garden) should be clustered
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1924_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1924_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1924_Task6" name="VP Store Operations and Category Manager evaluate layout changes: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Store Operations and Category Manager evaluate layout changes: (a) cross-merchandising opportunities: place adhesives near lumber; place paint accessories near paint station; place safety equipment near power tools, (b) destination vs. impulse: destination categories (lumber, cement, tiles) at back of store to drive traffic past impulse categories (hardware, tools, accessories), (c) flow optimization: ensure logical customer path from entrance through departments to checkout, (d) test layout changes at 3–5 pilot stores before chain-wide rollout
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Category Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1924_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1924_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1924_Task7" name="Measure pilot results: (a) compare sales per sqm before and after layout change…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Measure pilot results: (a) compare sales per sqm before and after layout change at pilot stores, (b) compare customer satisfaction scores at pilot vs. control stores, (c) if positive: implement chain-wide in next seasonal reset (W1407)
Responsible (R): Market Research Analyst / VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1924_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1924_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1924_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1924_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-375 (ensure controlled execution — Product Category &amp; Shopper Research (PA-44.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: VP Store Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
